From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:21:46 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] ps1-canvas

PlayStation frames fill the 640x480 canvas: each column reads its source
column from a map rebuilt only when the frame width changes, so 320 and 640
are exact and 256 and 512 drop no column, and 240-line frames have their
rows doubled by copying the row above. The fill is its own path, chosen by
Platform::fills_canvas through HostExtra; copy_centred, shared with gpSP,
is untouched. On the host the fill takes under 0.1 ms a frame in a release
build.

Actual shows the 4:3 picture 1:1 at 640x480 in the middle of the 720x480
panel: the source rect reaches past the texture and the game and retro
shaders draw black there. Every 3:2 canvas keeps the whole texture, so no
other system changes. Stretch fills the panel. The polaroid fits a 4:3
thumbnail between black bars instead of cropping it, and a 3:2 thumbnail
fits exactly as before.
